       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. The usual adult starting dose is 2.5 to 5 mg. A dose this high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a typical starting or maintenance dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, a lower starting dose\n\nIf 50 mg is intended, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note documenting that you verified the dose. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
